    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-end="471" data-start="196"><strong data-end="232" data-start="196">Transport order management — TMS</strong><br data-end="235" data-start="232"/>Without a centralized TMS, transport orders come in by email, phone, and WhatsApp. Assignments are managed in spreadsheets, confirmations are sent as PDFs, and disputes are impossible to trace. Every shipment becomes a manual operation.</p><p data-end="709" data-start="473"><strong data-end="501" data-start="473">Route planning &amp; loading</strong><br data-end="504" data-start="501"/>Optimizing loads, assigning the right vehicles and drivers, and respecting customer delivery windows — without a dedicated tool, this work takes hours every morning and generates avoidable transport costs.</p><p data-end="938" data-start="711"><strong data-end="743" data-start="711">Fleet tracking &amp; maintenance</strong><br data-end="746" data-start="743"/>Mileage is recorded in notebooks, maintenance checks are forgotten, and breakdowns
      immobilize vehicles without warning. Without centralized tracking, fleet costs quickly become uncontrollable.</p><p data-end="1163" data-start="940"><strong data-end="973" data-start="940">Transport invoicing &amp; pricing</strong><br data-end="976" data-start="973"/>Invoicing based on weight, volume, distance, pricing zones, or each customer’s specific conditions — without a dedicated tool — is a constant source of errors and silently erodes margins.</p><p data-end="1379" data-start="1165"><strong data-end="1205" data-start="1165">Transport documents &amp; CMR compliance</strong><br data-end="1208" data-start="1205"/>Managing CMRs, delivery notes, and customs certificates on paper exposes the company to costly disputes. Digitalization has become both an operational and legal necessity.</p>
